# vvaharness/backends/harness/deepagents/exclude_tools.py

Middleware that removes named tools from every model request, so the model is not offered them. It only un-advertises: a forged call to a removed tool would still execute (that is what `PermitTools` is for).

Source: `vvaharness/backends/harness/deepagents/exclude_tools.py` (lines 1-63)
Executor: code
Called from: `redaction.py` read_only_middleware; `options/graph_builder.py:425-428` and `options/subagents.py:136-137` (delete-only exclusion)

// src: vvaharness/backends/harness/deepagents/exclude_tools.py:36-60
ExcludeTools(excluded) {
  // runs around every model call (synchronous and asynchronous alike)
  wrap_model_call(request, handler) {
    kept = request.tools where tool name (BaseTool.name or dict "name") not in excluded
    return handler(if (fewer tools kept) request with tools = kept else request)
  }
}
